<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I55ffbf2f91933cd447d6645a4b3851283c08b813" commit="a1f6c4ff2e2647c6041242ab111e794643a87bd7" commit_message="FROMLIST: thermal: Add support for hardware-tracked trip points  This adds support for hardware-tracked trip points to the device tree thermal sensor framework.  The framework supports an arbitrary number of trip points. Whenever the current temperature is updated, the trip points immediately below and above the current temperature are found. A .set_trips callback is then called with the temperatures. If there is no trip point above or below the current temperature, the passed trip temperature will be -INT_MAX or INT_MAX respectively. In this callback, the driver should program the hardware such that it is notified when either of these trip points are triggered. When a trip point is triggered, the driver should call `thermal_zone_device_update' for the respective thermal zone. This will cause the trip points to be updated again.  If .set_trips is not implemented, the framework behaves as before.  This patch is based on an earlier version from Mikko Perttunen &lt;mikko.perttunen@kapsi.fi&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50756 TEST=Build and boot on rk3399 kevin  Signed-off-by: Sascha Hauer &lt;s.hauer@pengutronix.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Cc: Zhang Rui &lt;rui.zhang@intel.com&gt; Cc: Eduardo Valentin &lt;edubezval@gmail.com&gt; Cc: linux-pm@vger.kernel.org (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9137873/) (Note: fixes the lock) Change-Id: I55ffbf2f91933cd447d6645a4b3851283c08b813 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346446 Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346446" owner_email="wxt@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/46/346446/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I0dc41ae6dfa0bfe9219cd64c379c6306aa892f98" commit="eedf35c12052f94a15f0ddc7df8238898aa9f9e4" commit_message="FROMLIST: thermal: of: implement .set_trips for device tree thermal zones  This patch implements .set_trips for device tree thermal zones. As the hardware-tracked trip points is supported by thermal core patch[0].  patch[0] &quot;thermal: Add support for hardware-tracked trip points&quot;.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50756 TEST=Build and boot on rk3399 kevin  Signed-off-by: Sascha Hauer &lt;s.hauer@pengutronix.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Cc: Zhang Rui &lt;rui.zhang@intel.com&gt; Cc: Eduardo Valentin &lt;edubezval@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Javi Merino &lt;javi.merino@arm.com&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9137875/) Change-Id: I0dc41ae6dfa0bfe9219cd64c379c6306aa892f98 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346447 Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346447" owner_email="wxt@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/47/346447/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I1b69aa226609dcb42c1c3f7650931daebe5b78b1" commit="70e86a5356574463b0df0cb84f17126aefbb1b88" commit_message="FROMLIST: thermal: streamline get_trend callbacks  The .get_trend callback in struct thermal_zone_device_ops has the prototype:         int (*get_trend) (struct thermal_zone_device *, int,                           enum thermal_trend *); whereas the .get_trend callback in struct thermal_zone_of_device_ops has:         int (*get_trend)(void *, long *);  Streamline both prototypes and add the trip argument to the OF callback aswell and use enum thermal_trend * instead of an integer pointer.  While the OF prototype may be the better one, this should be decided at framework level and not on OF level.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50756 TEST=Build and boot on rk3399 kevin  Signed-off-by: Sascha Hauer &lt;s.hauer@pengutronix.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Cc: Zhang Rui &lt;rui.zhang@intel.com&gt; Cc: Eduardo Valentin &lt;edubezval@gmail.com&gt; Cc: linux-pm@vger.kernel.org (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9137877/) Change-Id: I1b69aa226609dcb42c1c3f7650931daebe5b78b1 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346448 Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346448" owner_email="wxt@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/48/346448/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I018497fcb6da97d1473672e869a08f1fc20bd6d9" commit="57679671d38001f853f8be2623a64c81a133bbed" commit_message="FROMLIST: thermal: bang-bang governor: act on lower trip boundary  With interrupt driven thermal zones we pass the lower and upper temperature on which shall be acted, so in the governor we have to act on the exact lower temperature to be consistent. Otherwise an interrupt maybe generated on the exact lower temperature, but the bang bang governor does not react since The polling driven zones have to be one step cooler before the governor reacts.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50756 TEST=Build and boot on rk3399 kevin  Signed-off-by: Sascha Hauer &lt;s.hauer@pengutronix.de&gt; Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Cc: Zhang Rui &lt;rui.zhang@intel.com&gt; Cc: Eduardo Valentin &lt;edubezval@gmail.com&gt; Cc: linux-pm@vger.kernel.org Acked-by: Peter Feuerer &lt;peter@piie.net&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9137883/) Change-Id: I018497fcb6da97d1473672e869a08f1fc20bd6d9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346449 Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346449" owner_email="wxt@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/49/346449/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I50eca84de1bdbcb366ce3a922d299f6e61d8d1e3" commit="185c417c2963bf20247446f877d3add790e6cbc3" commit_message="FROMLIST: thermal: rockchip: add the set_trips function  Whenever the current temperature is updated, the trip points immediately below and above the current temperature are found. A sensor driver callback `set_trips' is then called with the temperatures. Lastly, The sensor will trigger the hardware high temperature interrupts to increase the sampleing rate and throttle frequency to limit the temperature rising When performing passive cooling.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50756 TEST=Build and boot on rk3399 kevin  Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Cc: Zhang Rui &lt;rui.zhang@intel.com&gt; Cc: Eduardo Valentin &lt;edubezval@gmail.com&gt; Cc: linux-pm@vger.kernel.org (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9137885/) Change-Id: I50eca84de1bdbcb366ce3a922d299f6e61d8d1e3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346450 Reviewed-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="346450" owner_email="wxt@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/50/346450/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1c91d61b7828f82a2b39262bb5bcae786f38328c" commit="9540fbef021054722a0e06e899f0046b85dcdd2d" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iio: cros_ec: Trigger needs ops data  Although generally optionial, trig-&gt;ops is required if the driver trig is defined in is compiled as a module.  BUG=b:27849483 TEST=Without it, crash when setting the cros_ec_ring trigger.  Change-Id: I1c91d61b7828f82a2b39262bb5bcae786f38328c Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341510 Reviewed-by: Dmitry Torokhov &lt;dtor@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="341510" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/10/341510/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I583cdc4afc5d406a3e4ab7e0ddc5caff1b42ff24" commit="df94179209954a76b576ef89e968deac77a7ff09" commit_message="CHROMIUM: cros_ec: Fix module loading issues.  Name of the driver in the C code was not matching their Makefile names. This prevented the drivers from loaded as module. Also, export _mec entry points to allow the lpc module to use these function.  BUG=none TEST=Load when compiled as module.  Change-Id: I583cdc4afc5d406a3e4ab7e0ddc5caff1b42ff24 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/341673 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="341673" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/341673/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I91bd3e9eac435f059f44059e9b9c8aa57ffdae28" commit="ff15361fc3aed82f765b4f08666b4fbdd74483f0" commit_message="CHROMIUM: iio: cros_ec: Allow cros_ec_sensors_ring to load as a module  Use IS_ENABLED to compile code when _ring module is compile within the kernel or as a module.  BUG=none TEST=Check the sensors s